;; Verified public-register citations for the legal entity archived by this
;; repository.
;;
;; Every row in :catalog/entries is checked live by tools/verify_citations.cljk:
;;   * GET :cite/url must answer HTTP 2xx
;;   * :cite/expect-substring must appear in the response body
;;
;; The substring is the point. A 2xx alone says the host answered SOMETHING —
;; a login wall, a bot challenge and a data feed all return one. Each substring
;; below is a claim ABOUT THIS ENTITY, so a citation that stops carrying it is
;; DRIFT and fails the gate rather than passing as "reachable".
;;
;; Independent third-party archive. Not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
;; sponsored by PLDT Inc.

{:catalog/subject
 {:company/legal-name   "PLDT Inc."
  :company/lei          "254900ADE8GQHM5P2648"
  :company/jurisdiction "PH"
  :company/registered-as "PW00000055"
  :company/legal-form-elf "WHGH"
  :company/registration-authority "RA000483"
  :company/managing-lou "5493001KJTIIGC8Y1R12"
  :company/website      "https://pldthome.com/"}

 :catalog/retrieved "2026-08-20T07:05:00Z"

 ;; The floor the gate holds this catalogue to, declared beside the rows it
 ;; guards rather than left to a flag default. A catalogue quietly emptied of
 ;; its rows must not pass as "everything checked", and a floor far below the
 ;; real count would have to lose most of the catalogue before it noticed.
 :catalog/min-citations 11

 ;; ── what could NOT be cited, and why ────────────────────────────────────────
 ;;
 ;; This is not an omission. The repository's own provenance claim points at a
 ;; URL that no longer serves the document, and a catalogue that simply left it
 ;; out would read as though nobody had looked.
 :catalog/uncitable
 [{:cite/url "https://pldthome.com/privacypolicy"
   :cite/why :bot-challenge
   :cite/observed {:http-status 247
                   :served "JavaScript challenge interstitial (Reblaze), not the policy"
                   :checked "2026-08-20T07:00:32Z"}
   :cite/note
   "This is the :source-url of the archive in this repository (README, and the
    entry in 80-data/public/tos.journal.edn retrieved 2026-07-25T06:36:08Z).
    It answers a bot-protection challenge now, so the archived text can no
    longer be re-derived from the URL it names. The archived bytes and their
    SHA-256 remain the record; what is gone is independent re-retrieval.

    NOT worked around. Defeating a bot check to make a citation green would
    make the gate say something the open web does not, and the point of the
    gate is that it says only what the open web says."}]

